<title>USA: Mass. Gov still wants casino gambling - paper.</title>
<headline>Mass. Gov still wants casino gambling - paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Massachusetts Gov William Weld said on Tuesday that he will again ask the legislature to authorize two casinos.</p>
<p>The measure would also permit hundreds of slot machines at race tracks in Massachusetts.</p>
<p>But Weld faces criticism for the proposal from Attorney General Scott Harshbarger. Harshbarger claims the casinos will lead to more organized crime in the state.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
</text>
